      "message": "```suggestion\nenum class ModuleRemoval {\n```\n...so that:\n\n- the namespace is not cluttered with a generic name `Default`,\n- this thing is type-safe,\n- you will catch the bug introduced in PS17 where the C++ value `Default` is `force \u003d 0`, which (hopefully) means \"do not remove module if other depend on it\", but then you have an enum value `FailOnDependencies` which actually is `force \u003d 1`, and therefore it actually means \"remove any moduels which depend on this one as well\".",
