      "writtenOn": "2026-07-15T08:08:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The actual meaning of this flag is still the opposite of what the C documentation is saying. The upstream library takes `1` to mean \"drop this module and all modules which depend on it\". You implemented a C++ wrapper, where saying `Default` does this non-default thing, and saying `FailOnDependencies` makes the wrapper **not** fail on dependencies, but to remove them. This is not good, as I pointed out in my previous comment.\n\n\nThis also means that this feature needs proper testing, so, please, add tests which check what happens when you try to uninstall module A when there\u0027s module B which depends on it.",
      "parentUuid": "5a626887_5d15b9f7",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 213,
        "startChar": 0,
